   "access_tier": "public",
   "codebook_declared_type": "text",
   "description": "The most final thing that happened to this bill, read from its FULL Congress.gov action history rather than from its latest action alone. Values, most final first: `enacted`; `veto-overridden`; `vetoed`; `passed-both-chambers-not-enacted` (presented to the President, no law); `passed-one-chamber`; `floor-vote-failed`; `withdrawn`; `reported-from-committee-never-voted` (a committee said yes and the floor never called it up); `referred-and-died-in-committee` (no committee ever reported it); `pending-in-committee` (same shape, but the Congress is still sitting so no death can be inferred); `floor-vote-held-outcome-unresolved`; `unclassified`; `no-action-record`. The last is NOT a death - it means no action record was obtainable, which is a statement about our evidence and not about the bill. The two committee categories are the ones latest_action alone cannot tell apart, and they are different political facts.",
   "examples": [
    "enacted",
    "passed-one-chamber",
    "no-action-record",
    "floor-vote-held-outcome-unresolved",
    "floor-vote-failed",
    "vetoed",
    "referred-and-died-in-committee",
    "committee-acted-never-reported",
    "superseded-by-another-measure",
    "placed-on-calendar-never-voted",
    "reported-from-committee-never-voted",
    "pending-in-committee"
   ],
